Given OfficeSupplies
  team: Team
  supplies: Supply[]

Given Supply
  name: Text required
  quantity: Number optional
  status: available | needingRestock = available

When member adds a supply
  require member belongs to OfficeSupplies.team
  create Supply with status available

When member edits a supply
  require member belongs to OfficeSupplies.team
  update its name and quantity

When member marks a supply as needing restock
  require member belongs to OfficeSupplies.team
  set its status to needingRestock

When member marks a supply as available
  require member belongs to OfficeSupplies.team
  set its status to available

When member removes a supply
  require member belongs to OfficeSupplies.team
  delete it

Then Office Supplies
  visible to members of OfficeSupplies.team

  search supplies by name

  view all supplies
  view available supplies
  view supplies needing restock

  show count of supplies in the current view

  show a create form for name and optional quantity

  show each supply's name, quantity, and status
  allow members to edit, change status, and remove each supply

  when the current view has no supplies
    show "No supplies here yet. Add a supply to get started."

## Behavior example: a successful edit
## Given a team member edits "Printer paper" and sets quantity to 12
## When the edit is submitted
## Then "Printer paper" has quantity 12

## Behavior example: a nonmember is denied
## Given a person who is not a member of the team
## When they try to view or change its supplies
## Then access is denied
